If an image is generated within a servlet file, you need to create a separate servlet to handle the image generation and output. Then, you can reference the servlet in your HTML file's `img` tag.

Here's a simple example:

1. Create a servlet that generates and sends an image as a response:

```java
import javax.imageio.ImageIO;
import javax.servlet.ServletException;
import javax.servlet.annotation.WebServlet;
import javax.servlet.http.HttpServlet;
import javax.servlet.http.HttpServletRequest;
import javax.servlet.http.HttpServletResponse;
import java.awt.*;
import java.awt.image.BufferedImage;
import java.io.IOException;

@WebServlet(name = "ImageServlet", urlPatterns = { "/generated-image" })
public class ImageServlet extends HttpServlet {

    @Override
    protected void doGet(HttpServletRequest request, HttpServletResponse response)
            throws ServletException, IOException {

        // Create a BufferedImage with a specific size and color
        int width = 200;
        int height = 200;
        BufferedImage image = new BufferedImage(width, height, BufferedImage.TYPE_INT_RGB);
        Graphics2D graphics = image.createGraphics();
        graphics.setColor(Color.blue);
        graphics.fillRect(0, 0, width, height);

        // Set the response content type to "image/jpeg" or "image/png" based on the image format
        response.setContentType("image/jpeg");

        // Write the image to the response output stream
        ImageIO.write(image, "jpeg", response.getOutputStream());

        // Close the output stream explicitly
        response.getOutputStream().close();
    }
}
```

2. Reference the servlet in your HTML file using the `img` tag:

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
    <title>Generated Image Example</title>
</head>
<body>
    <h1>Generated Image:</h1>
    <img src="generated-image" alt="My Generated Image" />
</body>
</html>
```

In this example, the servlet is mapped to the URL pattern `/generated-image`, which is then used as the `src` attribute for the `img` tag in the HTML file. The servlet will generate a simple blue square image and return it as the response, displaying it in the HTML file.
